    "## 7. Summary & Insights <a id='summary'></a>\n",
    "\n",
    "### Key SQL Techniques Used\n",
    "\n",
    "| Technique | Purpose | Used In |\n",
    "|---|---|---|\n",
    "| **Subquery** | Filter rows based on aggregated values | Above-avg sales, max order per customer |\n",
    "| **CTE** | Reusable named result sets for cleaner queries | Customer totals, category summary |\n",
    "| **ROW_NUMBER()** | Assign unique rank within a partition | Orders ranked per customer |\n",
    "| **RANK() / DENSE_RANK()** | Rank with gap / without gap on ties | Customer sales ranking |\n",
    "| **SUM() OVER (...)** | Running totals across ordered rows | Cumulative daily sales |\n",
    "| **JOIN** | Combine normalized tables | All business queries |\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "### 📊 Business Insights\n",
    "\n",
    "1. **Top Customers Drive Revenue** — A small group of customers contributes disproportionately to total sales. Loyalty programs for top-ranked customers can protect this revenue.\n",
    "\n",
    "2. **Single-Order Customers = Retention Risk** — A significant number of customers placed only one order, signaling missed opportunities for repeat engagement.\n",
    "\n",
    "3. **High Discounts ≠ High Profit** — Sub-categories with the highest average discounts often show negative or minimal profit, suggesting discount strategies need revisiting.\n",
    "\n",
    "4. **Regional Variation** — Certain regions outperform others in both sales and profit margin. Region-specific campaigns could improve underperforming areas.\n",
    "\n",
    "5. **Above-Average Orders** — Orders exceeding the average sales value are concentrated in Technology and Furniture categories, which are high-value segments worth targeting.\n"
   ]
